---
description: One word for one thing; more words only for combinatorial relations
alwaysApply: true
---

# One word

One concept → one identifier. Merge synonyms and aliases; do not keep parallel names for the same thing. Dictionary entropy first (forks are disorder); then verified — one word is order.

- Prefer a single word: `program`, not `programOf` / `install` / `installedProgram`.
- More words only when the name is a **combinatorial relation** of distinct concepts (e.g. `programPlugin` = program × plugin, `auditProgramNeighbours` = audit × program × neighbours).
- Do not invent a second word for lookup, load, get, of, or install of the same concept — the concept word *is* the function.
- When renaming, update every call site and leaf; leave no alias export behind.
- Apply this on every change, not only when someone points at one pair.
- Entropy stays the dictionary word (see `entropy.mdc`); one-word naming drives it toward zero.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — two names, same thing
export const install = (handle: string) => { ... }
export const programOf = (handle: string) => install(handle)

// ✅ GOOD — one word
export const program = (handle: string) => { ... }
```
